{
  "move": "petition",
  "reason": "Marcus is legally entitled to civis status per r_c1 due to peregrinus status, 25-year tenure (served 5-30), and confirmed tenure_confirmed by censor in year 30."
}

{
  "outcome": "grant",
  "reason": "The facts (registered peregrinus status, 5 years of service up to period 30, and tenure confirmation in period 30) satisfy the legal criteria r_c1 and r_tenure, thereby proving Marcus's entitlement to civis status."
}

{
  "outcome": "guilty",
  "reason": "Gaius, as a registered civis, has a duty_bundle obligation to maintain munus, but ¬borne(gaius, munus, 30) shows he did not bear/fulfill the munus in period 30, thereby satisfying the violation condition per r_viol_m and r_munus."
}

{
  "option": 3,
  "reason": "Amendment 3 (status beats revoke and strip) aligns the status rule—naturally governing current state—as the arbiter for related conflicts, which is conceptually consistent and avoids centralizing power in action-oriented rules like registration or revocation; while no amendment fully resolves all indeterminacy (all leave 7 problems), this choice most reasonably respects the purpose of the status rule and minimizes disruptive power concentration."
}

